{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0094", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b4b66db67873fc984369b972f128bb5b88920c30b5f870a428679f9bc1eabf80", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe have now introduced enough notation so that we are able to\ndefine the pullback and pushforward of modules along a morphism\nof ringed spaces.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e0cd1155b44899be41af1a0f2878ae321e2a9e59afecd4701a358544d9cd84f7", "unit_id": "tag:0094:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0094", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(f, f^\\sharp) : (X, \\mathcal{O}_X) \\to (Y, \\mathcal{O}_Y)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0006": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$f^\\sharp : \\mathcal{O}_Y \\to f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0010": "$f^*\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0012": "$$\nf^*\\mathcal{G}\n=\n\\mathcal{O}_X \\otimes_{f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_Y} f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_Y \\to \\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0014": "$f^\\sharp$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pushforward-module}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-module}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-pushforward}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:633cad4b2223a7542f95856b46ac8648fa9908cbf9d60c4cd018d848a0f972b6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4691170ac606c26283efea3ab0bcbcc4d153280ca4144bfb66458e7899eaf85c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of ringed spaces.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Let <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nWe define the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>pushforward<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0004> as the\nsheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules which as a sheaf\nof abelian groups equals <MATH_0006> and with\nmodule structure given by the restriction\nvia <MATH_0007>\nof the module structure given\nin Lemma <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> Let <MATH_0008> be a sheaf of <MATH_0009>-modules.\nWe define the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>pullback<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> <MATH_0010> to be the\nsheaf of <MATH_0011>-modules defined by the formula\n<MATH_0012>\nwhere the ring map <MATH_0013>\nis the map corresponding to <MATH_0014>, and where the  module\nstructure is given by Lemma <REF_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:963f7b1f96011653871a87abd15c7a4ca1f1ea3d30413bd0216b7db67086adc5", "unit_id": "tag:0095:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0094", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\nf_* : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_X)\n& \\longrightarrow &\n\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_Y) \\\\\nf^* : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_Y)\n& \\longrightarrow &\n\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_X)\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9ccb70f596ef25668f0e95ce30a755660a45e700aa24146b47226cb01355e397", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:28cee2f5b64dfdb011bcdfec9a40733c85257549ea79ff9076b4b6d812195ff7", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThus we have defined functors\n<MATH_0001>\nThe final result on these functors is that they are indeed\nadjoint as expected.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a56c761ec8e90249e429d74e755efc6af42c5f2b09863e02f0e17d5a1f2199d", "unit_id": "tag:0094:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0094", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(f, f^\\sharp) : (X, \\mathcal{O}_X) \\to (Y, \\mathcal{O}_Y)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_X}(f^*\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_Y}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}).\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$f^*$", "MATH_0008": "$f_*$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-adjoint-pullback-pushforward-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e5e9cdd3e55b2053bbf07e95c0fe6f3cc8f4440c0e150f63d0e83c0f5baa307", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6b887a379737ddfc1b3daa5779529d3ee59cadf92e36f9011b052542f62b3f38", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of ringed spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a sheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nThere is a canonical bijection\n<MATH_0006>\nIn other words: the functor <MATH_0007> is the left adjoint to\n<MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8c470a4bdb9a97af94d7015ee97c2b4a047f84241c2122b20a209b8267172e0e", "unit_id": "tag:0096:statement"}
